{"nodes": [{"id": "changelog_002_rule_evaluator", "label": "Changelog 002 \u2014 Rule Evaluator sandboxado", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/changelog/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Diverg\u00eancia do spec reportada: json-logic trocado por json-logic-qubit porque o pacote citado pela pr\u00f3pria spec est\u00e1 quebrado em Python 3 \u2014 exatamente o tipo de coisa que 'hard rules que mais doem corrigir depois se nascerem inseguras' descreve; sem rodar teste nenhum, o rule_evaluator teria uma depend\u00eancia que quebra em toda chamada. Valida\u00e7\u00e3o: ruff limpo, pytest 18 passed (11 anteriores + 7 novos)."}, {"id": "changelog_002_rule_evaluator_rule_evaluator_py", "label": "mcp_engine/core/rule_evaluator.py \u2014 evaluate(ruleset, facts)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/changelog/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Percorre ruleset.rules na ordem do YAML; a primeira regra cujo condition avalia truthy decide o effect. Nenhuma regra casa \u2192 RuleDecision(effect=ALLOW). Condi\u00e7\u00e3o malformada levanta RuleEvaluationError(rule_id, cause) em vez de ser ignorada ou tratada como DENY silencioso."}, {"id": "changelog_002_rule_evaluator_ruledecision", "label": "RuleDecision (models.py)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/changelog/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Campos effect, rule_id, message; _StrictModel como os demais (frozen, extra=forbid) \u2014 imut\u00e1vel."}, {"id": "changelog_002_rule_evaluator_ruleevaluationerror", "label": "RuleEvaluationError", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/changelog/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_002_rule_evaluator_json_logic_qubit", "label": "json-logic-qubit (depend\u00eancia adotada)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/changelog/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://github.com/qubitproducts/json-logic-py", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fork mantido recomendado pelos pr\u00f3prios mantenedores do reposit\u00f3rio original nas issues. Mesmo nome de m\u00f3dulo e fun\u00e7\u00e3o (from json_logic import jsonLogic) \u2014 zero mudan\u00e7a no design do rule_evaluator.py al\u00e9m do nome do pacote no pyproject.toml."}, {"id": "changelog_002_rule_evaluator_json_logic", "label": "json-logic 0.6.3 (PyPI, quebrado em Python 3)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/changelog/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Usa tests.keys()[0], sintaxe v\u00e1lida em Python 2 mas n\u00e3o em Python 3 \u2014 TypeError: 'dict_keys' object is not subscriptable em qualquer uso; issue aberta desde 2017 no upstream, nunca corrigida na vers\u00e3o publicada. O pacote citado pela pr\u00f3pria spec est\u00e1 quebrado, n\u00e3o \u00e9 peculiaridade deste projeto."}, {"id": "changelog_002_rule_evaluator_test_rule_evaluator", "label": "tests/test_rule_evaluator.py (7 casos)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/changelog/002-rule-evaluator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cobre: ALLOW/DENY/REQUIRE_APPROVAL quando a regra casa, first-match-wins com duas regras conflitantes, default ALLOW sem match, RuleSet vazio cai no default, condi\u00e7\u00e3o malformada levanta RuleEvaluationError com o rule_id certo, RuleDecision imut\u00e1vel."}], "edges": [{"source": "changelog_002_rule_evaluator", "target": "docs_readme_changelog_dir", "relation": "conceptually_related